first class i actually attended was a  class called transformative design at  the d-school i never knew about design  thinking but i heard about lots of good  things about the classes at the d-school  and i decided to check it out and this  class which i chose as my first class  was really aimed at teaching students  design thinking and using it to rethink  their personal relationships and also  rethink their career trajectory they've  also got pop-outs which are kind of  five-week courses that you go out for  instance i did one with the bank of the  west we literally went in san francisco  and brainstormed for them and gave them  some solutions going forward for finance  post-disaster it's been one of my  transformations actually this year and  just way different ways of thinking in  different ways of brainstorming it  managed my expectations about my fear  about not being able to find a job when  i go back to singapore and it helped me  think about more deeply and recognize  that it was due to my lack of  self-confidence  and it gave me lots of tools and  ways to think about how i can pursue  opportunities to address this fear i  also felt like i learned a lot about  design thinking and really enjoyed the  whole design thinking process  and so much so that now i'm pursuing new  opportunities in design thinking as a  next curious step when i go back to  singapore
 

